1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,604
Once water goes in, a clock starts.

2
00:00:02,604 --> 00:00:03,554
Here's why.

3
00:00:03,554 --> 00:00:07,343
Inside a sealed vial, the peptide is a dry powder.

4
00:00:07,343 --> 00:00:08,398
Freeze-dried.

5
00:00:08,398 --> 00:00:09,895
Almost nothing moves.

6
00:00:09,895 --> 00:00:12,265
No water, no reactions.

7
00:00:12,265 --> 00:00:14,127
The molecule is on pause.

8
00:00:14,127 --> 00:00:15,520
Then water goes in.

9
00:00:15,520 --> 00:00:17,109
And everything changes.

10
00:00:17,109 --> 00:00:22,252
The molecules can move again, and the chemistry that water enables comes back with them.

11
00:00:22,252 --> 00:00:25,559
Dry powder and solution are two different worlds.

12
00:00:25,559 --> 00:00:26,992
One is built to wait.

13
00:00:26,992 --> 00:00:28,606
The other is free to move.

14
00:00:28,606 --> 00:00:30,716
That is the moment the clock starts.

15
00:00:30,716 --> 00:00:31,953
Follow us for more.

